{
  "_comment": "Abbreviation Helper configuration. The copy in your Zotero data directory (abbreviation-helper/abbreviations.json) is yours to edit; entries there win over these defaults. Sections: userDefs = your own abbreviation -> meaning entries, always shown even if the paper defines the term differently. ignore = abbreviations to never display. databases = lookup links ({q} = token with hyphens removed, {raw} = token as written); if your file defines a non-empty databases list it replaces this one entirely. staticDefs and commonKnownDefs are the curated defaults: staticDefs only normalises definitions a paper already provides, commonKnownDefs is a fallback glossary for well-known abbreviations a paper uses without defining (ambiguity medium/high entries additionally require one of their context words to appear in the document).",
  "userDefs": {},
  "ignore": [],
  "databases": [
    {
